Rule 1 (The number of indices should not exceed the dimension of input tensor, and the data type of value tensor should match the data type of input tensor.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : list(tensor), v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ v_2.len ∧ dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_3)
>>
Rule 2 (If the input tensor is empty, then the value tensor should be empty too.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0 then ∃j ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, j) = 0
>>
Rule 3 (If the index is out of bounds, the shape of the indexed tensor should be 0 along that dimension.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : tensor} |= if min(v_3) < 0 ∨ max(v_3) ≥ shape(v_1, v_2) then shape(v_1, v_2) = 0
>>
Rule 4 (The data type of the elements of the index tensor should be int.)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 2 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 4 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 5
